# Allowlist: exclude everything, then re-include exactly what the Dockerfile
# copies. Patterns match the full relative path, so a directory rule never
# matches the files inside it — each tree needs both `dir` and `dir/**`. Last
# match wins, so re-exclusions come after the re-include that covered them.
*

# --- Python build inputs (python-builder; the Console's build is package data in src/) ---
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src
!src/**

# --- The example looks (runtime: `COPY examples/*.look.json`) ---
!examples
!examples/*.look.json

# --- Junk that would otherwise ride along inside the allowlisted trees ---
**/__pycache__
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store

# --- Secrets, databases and caches that a developer's tree may hold inside
# the allowlisted trees (the Python wheel would ship them) ---
**/.env*
**/*.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.sqlite3*
**/*.db
**/.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache/**
